messages:
alice-plat: anyone else seeing a flurry of ECONNRESETs from clients using the sidecar proxy? console still shows streams as ACTIVE :confused;
bob-sre: saw that at 10:23 UTC, spikes of ~200 resets in 2m. console shows connection count steady, no ERROR tags;
carol-console: which sidecar pool? any specific route/tenant?;
dave-infra: edge-sidecar-1; appears to be idle-timeout enforcement closing the socket while upstream still has open stream record;
eve-telemetry: our stream-close sampling is 5% so this will frequently be missed in traces. if we don't capture it, console will keep the connection state as open;
alice-plat: client logs show immediate ECONNRESET after keepalive; server logs show `conn_id=42 state=OPEN -> FIN_RCVD` then a `RST` being written;

[log snippet]
[2026-03-23T10:23:12Z] edge-sidecar-1 conn=42 read_timeout
[2026-03-23T10:23:12Z] edge-sidecar-1 conn=42 send RST
[2026-03-23T10:23:12Z] router upstream conn=42 still streaming

bob-sre: that pattern -> sidecar kills socket (half-close) but our control plane marks session open because it never saw the final close event;
carol-console: UX problem: console health widget shows active streams and SLOs look fine -> support will get ticketed. We should show "ambiguous" state when telemetry for stream-close is missing;
dave-infra: also noticed billing/quota system counts every reconnect as a new session; customers saw quota bumps from this surge. so now it's reliability + cost exposure;
eve-telemetry: short-term: increase stream-close sampling for edge-sidecar pool to 100% for 1h and capture traces (abc123 from alice is helpful);

alice-plat: long-term: two parts: 1) sidecar should publish explicit `STREAM_CLOSED` event to control plane before tearing down sockets; 2) console needs an inferred-state when telemetry samples are absent (e.g., mark stream as "unknown/closing");
bob-sre: agree. we can also make router update session TTL on a FIN/RST path so console decays faster instead of staying green;
carol-console: UX change proposal: show a yellow "stale" badge if last-close-timestamp > 15s and no close-event seen. Also surface sampling rate on the stream detail panel;
dave-infra: deployment concern: sidecar change requires canary; we should avoid double-counting during rollout. routing policy should fallback to keepalive-based soft-close until new event is available;
eve-telemetry: actions: 1) temp bump sampling -> analytics (i) collect all close events 2) add trace tag on recon a/b tests 3) emit metric `stream_close_inferred` when we detect FIN but miss close-event;
deploy-bot: rolling canary job queued: canary=edge-sidecar-1:2 -> 10% -> 50% if no new errors. tag: sidecar-stream-close-emit-20260323;
alice-plat: OK i'll file infra PR for explicit event + router TTL bump. carol, can you draft console badge copy? bob, coordinate SRE on canary watch;
carol-console: will do, draft in #eng-platform-design and ping product for wording;
bob-sre: i'll watch the canary and set alert on `reconnect_rate` and `quota_charge_delta` for impacted tenants;
dave-infra: note: also add a migration step in billing to dedupe reconnections within 5s window to avoid charging during rollout;
neal: (out-of-band) adding a small note: we should also consider backfilling missing close-events in analytics for the last 24h for incident review;
alice-plat: thanks everyone. follow-ups: eve bump sampling now, bob watch canary, dave billing dedupe change, carol UX copy. keep thread updates here :thumbsup:
